      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "As-solidified CoCrFeMnNi has a homogeneous solid-solution microstructure.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6093928::chunk::001::introduction::2dc33c3a9e",
        "PMC7229066::chunk::000::abstract::33b9dea56c"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Co-free FeNiCrMn derivative has a homogeneous as-solidified solid-solution microstructure.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Removing Co from equiatomic CoCrFeMnNi reduces stacking-fault energy.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Removing Co modifies short-range chemical ordering.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced stacking-fault energy and modified short-range order alter dislocation nucleation and mobility.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Co removal shifts the dominant deformation mechanism toward a lower-energy, thermally activated dislocation-motion regime.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The altered chemical environment in Co-free FeNiCrMn lowers the energy barrier for dislocation nucleation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The absence of Co promotes more efficient thermally activated dislocation motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Earlier or faster dislocation activity stabilizes the strength–ductility trade-off under dynamic loading.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Co-free FeNiCrMn maintains a favorable strength–ductility balance across a broad range of temperatures and strain rates.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic CoCrFeMnNi has a favorable strength–ductility combination, including at low temperatures.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6093928::chunk::001::introduction::2dc33c3a9e",
        "PMC7512559::chunk::001::introduction::316f02dec2"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to CoCrFeMnNi, Co-free FeNiCrMn will have a lower yield-stress threshold for initiating dislocation motion.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The reduction in the dislocation-initiation threshold will be especially evident where thermal activation is significant.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Co-free FeNiCrMn will exhibit dislocation-density evolution distinct from that of CoCrFeMnNi.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Co-free FeNiCrMn will exhibit slip activity distinct from that of CoCrFeMnNi.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The altered dislocation-density and slip evolution will correlate with improved ductility while preserving strength.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed mechanism applies from approximately 77 K to 700 °C and from 1×10^-4 to 1×10^-2 s^-1.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
